From 88e5af0764c8aa2c7d0bc8272c9de600ef77e54f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:10:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] constellation: report content processes that die from a
 signal

When a content process was killed (SIGSEGV, the OOM killer's SIGKILL) its
lifeline closed and the constellation merely reaped it, so the webview
kept its last frame forever. The process exit is now treated as a crash:
the event loop is retired (its pipelines are removed without waiting for
an acknowledgement that will never come, its hosts get a fresh process,
and its session-history documents reload on traversal), the embedder gets
the new WebViewDelegate::notify_content_process_terminated with the exit
status, and the crash page replaces the dead document. Send failures to a
content process are left to the lifeline so a crash is reported once, and
an embedder navigation now replaces Servo's crash page instead of being
dropped while that page is still loading.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
